# Project workflow

The user requested one ongoing working branch: `codex/project-work`.
Continue ordinary implementation, documentation and experiment work there.
Update its consolidated PR rather than creating a branch or PR per milestone.
Create another persistent branch only when the user explicitly requests one.

Before switching, use `git worktree list` to find the checkout holding that
branch and work in that directory. Preserve dirty files, ignored simulation
assets and all historical experiment data. Do not reset an existing checkout
or switch an open paper to a different file path.

After a material research decision, append a dated entry to
`docs/RESEARCH_DECISIONS.md`: previous plan, new evidence, choice, implementation
status and next check. Distinguish completed results, interpretations and
proposed experiments. Preserve original model/data/controller provenance;
scientific protocol versions remain distinct even though source shares a branch.

Keep `docs/PAPER_PROGRESS.md` and the working manuscript consistent with measured
claims. Compile the existing `.tex` source with the desktop compiler after edits.
